Definition of State of System
• Input output description applicable only for initially relaxed systems.
• Output depends not only on input but also on initial conditions.
State
The state of the system at time t0 is the amount of information at t0 that, together with u[t0,∞), determines uniquely the behavior of the system for all t ≥ t0.
• Behavior of system: All responses including system state
• State at any time summarizes the essential information about past inputs required for the prediction of future behavior.
• Different inputs might lead to the same state at a given time, but their future behavior would be the same for the same future inputs.
