Systems and State Vectors
• State vector: Finite-dimensional column vector that includes all information (variables) necessary for determining system behavior with known future inputs.
• State variables: Components of the state vector
• State space ∑: A linear space in which the state vector ranges.
Dynamical equations
The set of equations that describes the unique relations between the input, output, and state of the system. State and output equations:
x ̇ = h (x(t), u(t), t) , y = g (x(t), u(t), t)
Lumped and Distributed Systems
Lumped: Number of state variables is finite or its state is a finite vector Distributed: Infinitely many state variables
