Linearity of Dynamical Systems
• Necessary condition for linear system: {0, 0} → {0[t0,∞), 0[t0,∞)}
• With zero initial state and zero input, system responses are identically zero.
• Response of linear system due to {x(t0), u[t0,∞)}: Response due to {x(t0), 0} + Response due to {0, u[t0,∞)}
• Zero input response: Response due to {x(t0), 0}
• Zero state response: Response due to {0, u[t0,∞)}
• For a linear dynamical system
h(x, u, t) = A(t)x(t) + B(t)u(t), g(x, u, t) = C(t)x(t + E(t)u(t)
x ̇ = h(x, u, t) = A(t)x(t + B(t)u(t), y = g(x, u, t) = C(t)x(t + E(t)u(t)
• Unique solution: Every entry of A(t) be a continuous function of t over (−∞, ∞)
• Linear time-varying (LTV) dynamical system
